{"assets":["/statement-assets/8ef05f354761ab1b8d99cb58fa5d4b57766599c43a11abe29008681fa6fc8b39.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"111","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Petya and Rectangle"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Little Petya loves playing with rectangles. Mom bought Petya a rectangle divided into cells "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" in size (containing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" rows, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" columns). Petya marked two different cells of the rectangle and now he is solving the following task:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"simple path"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" between those two cells as a sequence of distinct cells "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., ak"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ak"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the two marked cells. Besides, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" are side-neighboring cells of the path ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ i < k"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Let's denote the path length as number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the sequence length). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petya's task is to find the longest simple path's length and to print the path. Help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4 ≤ n, m ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of rows and the number of columns in the rectangle, correspondingly. The second line contains space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the coordinates of the first marked cell. The third line contains space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the coordinates of the second marked cell ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 < x1, x2 < n, 1 < y1, y2 < m, x1 ≠ x2, y1 ≠ y2"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The coordinates of a marked cell are a pair of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" represents the row's number and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" represents the column's number. The rows are numbered from top to bottom with consecutive integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". The columns are numbered from the left to the right by consecutive integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the marked cells are not positioned in one row or column."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print the length of the found path — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":". In the next lines print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs of integers, one per line — coordinates of the cells that constitute the found path in the order, in which they follow in the path (the path must go from cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1, y1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" to cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x2, y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If there are several solutions, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 4\n2 2\n3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"15\n2 2\n1 2\n1 1\n2 1\n3 1\n4 1\n4 2\n4 3\n4 4\n3 4\n2 4\n1 4\n1 3\n2 3\n3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The statement test is described in the picture: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8ef05f354761ab1b8d99cb58fa5d4b57766599c43a11abe29008681fa6fc8b39.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"111E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/111/problem/E"}